{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"4bd46a22356d66bf","name":"card_unit_fw_190_f8","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/NavalWarfare/units/card_unit_fw_190_f8","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"FW 190 F-9","text":"At the end of each enemy turn, deal 4 damage to their HQ if they did not deploy a unit.","flavorText":"The Focke-Wulf Fw 190 F-9 was a late-war German ground-attack aircraft, developed as the final variant in the Fw 190 F-series. Introduced in early 1945, it was based on the Fw 190 A-9 airframe but incorporated several enhancements tailored for close air support missions. Similar to F-8s and A-8s variants, it was fitted with a bulged canopy enhancing the pilots visibility, which was a critical factor during low-altitude operations. The aircraft was equipped with four underwing bomb racks allowing it to carry a substantial bomb load for ground-attack roles. While exact production numbers are uncertain, records indicate that 147 F-9s were built in January 1945, with additional units likely produced until the war's end, although documentation for subsequent months is incomplete. The Fw 190 F-9 served on both the Eastern and Western Fronts and provided crucial support to German ground forces during the final months of WWII. Its robust design and effective armament made it a formidable opponent in the ground-attack role, despite the challenging conditions faced by the Luftwaffe in 1945.","faction":"Germany","type":"fighter","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_fw_190_f8","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_fw_190_f8_title","SourceString":"FW 190 F-9","LocalizedString":"FW 190 F-9"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":4,"defense":5,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_fw_190_f8_text","SourceString":"At the end of each enemy turn, deal 4 damage to their HQ if they